WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:02.268
[mysterious music]

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:07.974
NARRATOR: The tongue of
western diamondback rattlesnake

00:00:08.041 --> 00:00:10.110
cautiously tastes the air.

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:16.783
She flicks airborne particles
against the roof of her mouth

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:24.023
to be analyzed, sorting
out potential food

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:32.432
from potential threat, like
this other icon of the Old West,

00:00:32.499 --> 00:00:35.168
and he's hungry himself.

00:00:35.235 --> 00:00:39.239
The roadrunner is
a tough old bird.

00:00:39.305 --> 00:00:41.775
You have to be when the
slithering lunch you've

00:00:41.841 --> 00:00:45.445
got your eye on could kill you.

00:00:45.512 --> 00:00:48.248
The queen of rattlers,
the western diamondback,

00:00:48.314 --> 00:00:51.117
is a recipe for
deadly indigestion.

00:00:51.184 --> 00:00:54.053
She's venomous enough
to kill a human,

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:58.191
but she's missing something
in this looming face-off--

00:00:58.258 --> 00:01:00.427
legs.

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:02.529
[caws]

00:01:02.595 --> 00:01:06.900
The roadrunner has
got serious legs,

00:01:06.966 --> 00:01:08.668
and he knows how to use them.

00:01:08.735 --> 00:01:11.638
[dramatic music]

00:01:11.704 --> 00:01:13.573
[chirping]

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:23.283
Native Americans
revered the roadrunner

00:01:23.349 --> 00:01:27.687
for its speed, strength,
and especially its courage.

00:01:46.206 --> 00:01:49.843
The bird circles,
spiraling in on its target.

00:01:49.909 --> 00:01:55.114
But the snake's not going
down without a fight.

00:01:55.181 --> 00:01:57.183
[rattles]

00:02:00.887 --> 00:02:03.890
The plan is to grab the
snake behind her head

00:02:03.957 --> 00:02:06.226
and bash the poor
girl's skull in.

00:02:29.115 --> 00:02:34.988
In this face-off, guts
versus venom is a draw,

00:02:35.054 --> 00:02:38.358
and our snake gets
away with her life.

